<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17921" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fĕnestro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		fenestra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to furnish with openings</i> or <i>windows</i> (rare; not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">media oculorum cornua fenestravit pupilla,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 55, § 148</span></i>
			. —In <i>part. perf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">valvata ac fenestrata triclinia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 8, § 29</span></i>
			 Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">singulae partes turris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					10, 19 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oportuit hominum pectora fenestrata et aperta
					esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3 praef.</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
